WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.398
Chapter 08 puts the pieces
together with one rule:

2
00:00:03.398 --> 00:00:07.563
align each flow's consistency
class with its transport class.

3
00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:11.888
Only authoritative writes and
in-region quorum ride the lean path,

4
00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.799
and neither crosses a
region synchronously.

5
00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:17.537
At the branch, four
patterns cover practice.

6
00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:22.138
A, the hairpin: assessed, but
every flow pays the detour.

7
00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:26.712
B, bare local breakout: not an
option in the TIC use case at all.

8
00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:29.957
C, governed local breakout,
an SD-WAN edge plus a

9
00:00:29.957 --> 00:00:33.800
nearby SASE point of presence:
the reference pattern.

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.112
D, agent-delivered SASE,
for small and roaming sites,

11
00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:41.425
if the point of presence is close
and agentless devices are covered.

12
00:00:41.425 --> 00:00:47.060
Five decisions carry most of the risk: one
writer per region; a written path policy,

13
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.517
which SC-7(4) already asks for;
the boundary change before cutover;

14
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:56.900
the governor protected before it carries
traffic; and the path made evidence.

15
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.880
Each fails quietly, so
each comes with a check.
